WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.839
My name's Oliver Emberton I'm the

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.839
Managing Director of Silktide and today

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:09.920
I'm going to be giving you a

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.920
roughly 50 minute talk on making

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.200
accessible web forms hopefully we'll

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.480
have a little time at the end for

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.880
questions maybe we skip that off but

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.680
we'll see how we do

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.920
so what are we going to cover today I'm

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.680
going to break it out into three key

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.359
areas for forms

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.199
the first section is going to be the

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.240
appearance of forms

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.480
the

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.599
design aspect if you will semantics

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.360
which is going to be looking a little

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.480
bit into the code we're going to spend

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.840
quite a bit of time there we're going to

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.840
go through some of the technical details

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.360
of accessible forms and then finally

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.320
we're going to look at the flow so the

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.160
flow is going to be the way that forms

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.520
actually operate kind of from start to

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.320
finish

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.360
so let's get started with appearance

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.320
so the first thing we're going to look

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:56.239
at is boundaries so this is a new

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.440
concept in wcag 2.1 that refers to the

00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:59.600
contrast

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.000
of form elements and specifically kind

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.080
of the whether or not you can

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.920
understand the boundary of a form

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.479
element and kind of identify where that

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.920
form element is and what what it is

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:13.040
so what we see here on the left-hand

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.360
side is a standard form field

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.159
for a name and this has relatively high

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.840
contrast this has a fairly thick black

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:21.600
border and on the right hand side we

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.960
have the same control but with a

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.640
slightly trendier softer edge sort of

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.640
shadow effect quite common nowadays

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.920
now under this requirement the the

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.560
second control would not be classed as

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.640
accessible because although you and i

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:42.479
may be able to perceive the edge of that

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.840
field not everyone can as we'll see

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:45.439
now one

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.200
key aspect of this

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:48.880
requirement is it's not all about adding

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.040
thick black borders to everything it's

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.079
just about making sure elements are

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.320
clear

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:56.799
so for example you might add a

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.799
background color around a field and that

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:01.040
would achieve the same requirement that

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:02.560
would make it apparent that there is a

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.840
field there

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.680
and that you can use it unfortunately in

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.239
this case i've actually tricked you

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.840
because that color green isn't quite

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:12.959
contrasting enough it looks like it is

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:15.760
but it isn't

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:18.480
under wcag that color is actually not

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.239
sufficiently differentiated from

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.400
white which it's adjacent to so you

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.200
would actually fail wk even though that

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.800
looks

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.959
i think to most people that might look

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.640
like oh yes that's really really clear

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:29.840
it wouldn't be and this is one of the

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.360
reasons why you actually need to get

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.120
into the detail and sometimes check

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.640
these things

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.480
so let's let's go for a few more

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.160
fields so quickly i've got a drop menu

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.480
i've got a check box i've got some kind

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.800
of five star rating widget and i've got

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.280
a toggle button at the bottom and all

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.760
four of those would actually fail under

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.840
this requirement purely down to their

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.760
contrast the green you saw on the

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.360
previous screen is not

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.200
contrasting sufficiently with the

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.720
white or the the kind of eggshell gray

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.720
around it

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.879
and if you were to compare this with say

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.720
a more accessible variant

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:04.480
here i've used a stronger more

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.120
differentiated color

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.360
i've used a sharper border and the

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:12.080
kind of the caray if you will on the the

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.760
drop down menu is clearer

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.080
and in particular things like the

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.920
text on I know this this distinction may

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.040
seem subtle like those two may look the

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.959
same to like a casual observer the

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.159
one on the right is substantially more

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:25.519
legible

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:28.000
and I can show you this if I was to

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:30.560
simulate some form of visual disability

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.080
so here what you're doing is we're

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.799
essentially just lowering the visual

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.879
contrast and blurring but

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:39.519
a lot of information is is completely

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:41.120
lost when this happens and many people

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:42.560
have vision that

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.760
from a functional perspective it may not

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.120
look like this but from a functional

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.280
perspective is equivalent to what you're

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.720
seeing here so

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.319
things like those toggle buttons being

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.599
completely lost you just have no idea

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:57.680
what's going on the final star on the

00:03:53.599 --> 00:04:00.000
star rating is basically invisible

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.280
and even that checkbox surprisingly may

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.680
may be

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.920
difficult or impossible to discern

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:08.159
there's actually a subtle

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.400
additional like double check here

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:12.080
which is was not apparent if I go back

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.920
the the stars

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.799
that you're seeing on the left actually

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.400
have to contrast twice so for most of

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:19.759
these things you're just worried about

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.120
you know like the checkbox does it

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.000
contrast with the surroundings but with

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:26.800
the stars the star needs to contrast

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:29.600
with the background if it's filled

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.160
but the unfilled star also needs to

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.080
contrast with the background and

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.680
with the filled star

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.000
so that's why you've got this kind of

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:40.800
thick border here it's not enough just

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.720
to make sure that this star is different

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.400
is you know sharp against the background

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:46.639
it also needs to be different against

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.759
the star next to it this is surprisingly

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:50.160
tricky it's one of the reasons why these

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:51.600
kind of controls are hard to pull off

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.600
um

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.840
so why do we care about all of this

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.759
well insufficient contrast prevents

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:59.520
people with low vision from using forms

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:02.000
completely right so if you have a visual

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.840
impairment a large

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.759
number of visual impairments will affect

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.880
you in a way that

00:05:05.759 --> 00:05:08.639
makes forms like this completely

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.800
unusable

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:13.360
and you can literally just discern it

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.639
from sight you can look at a form or a

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.800
tool can look at a form and can just

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:18.080
tell you yeah that's not gonna work so

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.520
a formula like the one you see here

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.759
on the left quite trendy quite tasty

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:27.039
quite fashionable unfortunately would

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:27.039
fail in all manner of ways

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:32.080
so moving on to labels now anyone who's

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.680
worked with accessible forms is probably

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.400
sick of this word but let's talk a

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.400
little bit about it so what is a

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.039
label and why do we care

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:44.320
well if we take a form like this one

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:47.440
we've got a clear label at the top

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:49.520
so the label is basically telling you

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.120
what needs to go in the field right so

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.280
in this case I'm after your email

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.720
address or maybe I'm after your name or

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:58.000
whatever

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.880
the placeholder is distinctly is text

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.520
that is inside the field and that when

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.639
you type inside the field that text goes

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.880
away

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:08.080
so it's a relatively modern invention i

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.960
mean I think it's like eight years old

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:13.680
now or something but placeholders

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:15.199
typically are a sort of fainter shade

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.360
of gray or something so they're like

00:06:15.199 --> 00:06:19.600
more subtle and they can provide

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.520
things like examples like you see here

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.360
an example of an email address

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.639
that at least in theory is what they

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.919
are and that's what you should be doing

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:27.919
but unfortunately a lot of people kind

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:30.400
of get them mixed up so

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:31.440
it's quite common to see a form like

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.120
this

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:37.600
where someone uses a placeholder in

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.759
order to do what a label should be doing

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.199
so in this case they put what you're

00:06:39.759 --> 00:06:43.120
supposed to be typing in you know you

00:06:41.199 --> 00:06:45.039
need to type in an email they put that

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.880
inside as a placeholder

00:06:45.039 --> 00:06:49.120
and there's a few problems here as you

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.759
saw a moment ago that kind of gray

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.800
text is basically invisible to a number

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:55.280
of people

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.360
and so they literally won't even see

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.840
it but also you've got the problem that

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.000
when you start typing in that field you

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:03.759
don't know what you're asked for anymore

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.120
so all right this was an email address

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:06.800
but as soon as I start typing in an

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.560
email address i've

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:10.880
lost that information I don't know I'm

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:13.840
being asked for an email address

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:16.160
in this case it may seem slightly

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.919
like pedantic like why would you care

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.160
but consider a slightly more elaborate

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:23.680
form like this so this form doesn't have

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:25.440
labels it just has placeholders and

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.120
because i've filled in some of that form

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.440
or maybe the form is automatically

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.400
filled in for me I can't see what the

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.919
labels are

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.520
so I can guess

00:07:31.919 --> 00:07:36.160
maybe that's asking me for the first

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:38.800
line of an address maybe a street name a

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.680
city but I don't actually know the only

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.520
way I could actually know what those

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.680
fields are is if I deleted the text

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.400
inside each one which is crazy and that

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:49.039
last four field I have no idea I mean is

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:52.240
that like the house number is that the

00:07:49.039 --> 00:07:53.199
the area code it's like that is it

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.720
happens that's actually the

00:07:53.199 --> 00:07:56.560
international dialing code for the phone

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.800
number but how could you possibly know

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.800
that so

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.720
for all of those reasons labels really

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:06.160
important design affordance you should

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:08.319
actually be making visible on the page

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.400
and there are many ways to present them

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:12.479
but these are the three most common very

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:14.960
quickly the first approach you put

00:08:12.479 --> 00:08:16.319
the the label on the top left the

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.479
second you tend to put it on the left

00:08:16.319 --> 00:08:21.199
hand side and the third you kind of

00:08:18.479 --> 00:08:24.240
inline it so this is often known as a

00:08:21.199 --> 00:08:26.639
like a floating label this is quite

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.720
trendy and modern at the moment

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:29.840
so let's just do a very quick comparison

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:33.279
um

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:35.360
so the first approach has an obvious

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:36.399
advantage which is if you're on a small

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.519
display

00:08:36.399 --> 00:08:42.159
it tends to fit it uses less space

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:44.720
basically or less width I should say so

00:08:42.159 --> 00:08:46.160
just if you this isn't necessarily

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.680
saying it has to go off the edge but it

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:51.440
gives you more room

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:53.600
if you imagine a wide field so

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:55.600
email is not very wide piece of text but

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.000
say you had something like postal

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.440
address or home address or whatever

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.720
that's a lot of text to fit on the left

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:04.880
hand side of the field so it's generally

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:07.120
better I would recommend to stick with

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:09.279
the label on the top left

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.279
that is not a w requirement just better

00:09:09.279 --> 00:09:12.880
practice it's also slightly less

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:14.640
scrolling for people if they do have to

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.640
zoom in and scroll it's slightly easier

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.360
to use the first one

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.959
the

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.640
other design option which is the kind of

00:09:18.959 --> 00:09:22.480
the floating label very trendy at the

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.920
moment like I said it's a bit of a

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.360
religious debate over whether or not

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:26.480
these are good or bad

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.240
um

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.000
generally they're treated with

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.640
skepticism in the accessibility

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.519
community the main problem with them is

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.760
it's typical that this the label text

00:09:35.519 --> 00:09:39.440
is smaller and harder to read

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.519
but I do think it is sometimes possible

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.959
to make it work like you've got here i

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:45.600
think that that email could be clear

00:09:42.959 --> 00:09:47.440
enough so

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.200
really matter of personal preference i

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:52.320
would say but just make sure people can

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.320
still read the label

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:56.240
why do we care well if you don't have a

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:58.399
label at all forms are completely

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.000
inaccessible I mean consider that

00:09:58.399 --> 00:10:02.839
yeah this form on the left-hand side you

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.600
wouldn't know what you're doing now

00:10:02.839 --> 00:10:07.360
without

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.880
visible labels there are ways to add

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.760
hidden labels which we'll look at in a

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.800
moment

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.480
but

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.079
generally it's kind of discouraged the

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.360
problem is labels are useful for

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:16.959
everyone

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.040
so unless you've got something like a

00:10:16.959 --> 00:10:20.240
one field search form or something i

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.920
would generally recommend adding a

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.800
visible label

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:26.399
and they are required for wkag so you

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:29.440
have to have a label in there somewhere

00:10:26.399 --> 00:10:31.519
even if it's an invisible one

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.120
right so moving on to something called

00:10:31.519 --> 00:10:35.519
focus so again this will be familiar for

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.760
the webs in the room

00:10:35.519 --> 00:10:40.399
this is a very simple form

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:42.560
and we have something called a focus

00:10:40.399 --> 00:10:44.800
state for all of these controls and what

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.200
that is is something like this where i

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.040
say select that first field maybe i

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.959
click inside it

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.560
or I go to the next field or I go to the

00:10:50.959 --> 00:10:54.000
next field and so you can you've seen

